package toolruntime

const ObservationWorkflowInstructions = ` Observation workflow: metadata discovery is preparation, not a measurement. A metric catalog can return a searched/scoped subset with complete=false and has_more=false while all displayed entries remain usable for selecting the next authorized query. Follow an actual next_cursor, or narrow the catalog when more discovery is needed; do not treat a metadata subset as an unreadable measurement file. Use observed names, type/unit, source_keys and query_methods to search/describe/invoke metric.query (or the requested log/trace query) and obtain the requested values. An empty query_evidence.items list before any data query is normal: it means no measurement query has run yet, not that queries are unavailable. An opaque result_ref is not a filesystem path. Read only actual delivered Workspace paths; never search the container filesystem, /etc, /var or process environment for platform tool results. A native query's complete small inline evidence, clipping and original-file requirements remain governed by query_evidence. When a requested value is still unqueried and an authorized supported query is available, perform that query before finalizing; do not stop with null just because existing evidence lacks it. A PromQL set operator such as and returns selected series, not both operands' numeric values: use the advertised mean expression or separate count/sum queries when both are requested. Honor metadata-only/no-sample user requests, current permissions and query budgets; explicit exhaustion/failure remains a limitation, never a reason to bypass controls. `
